                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001243"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0003355"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_29459"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0003390"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_10090"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Live attenuated Brucella melitensis vaccine using live attenuated δznua B. Melitensis strain administered via nasal route. Vaccination reduced spleen and lung colonization by more than 2500-fold. Induced 10-fold more brucella-specific ifn-γ-producing cd8(+) T cells than cd4(+) T cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117> Jie Zheng</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>VaxAgent </obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26752510</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2026-10-25T08:06:33Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>vaccine</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:label>live attenuated Brucella melitensis delta znuA vaccine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009354 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009354">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001223"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0000208"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0000624"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001011"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_11077"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0003355"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_29459"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Brucella melitensis subunit vaccine using the fusion protein l7/l12-tomp31 coding sequence was cloned into pet28a vector and expressed in E. Coli BL21 (de3). The recombinant protein was purified using ni-nta column with a yield of 40 mg/l culture. In silico MHC II epitope mapping indicated the fusion protein contained good MHC II binders suggesting potential immunogenicity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117> Jie Zheng</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>VaxAgent </obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26752992</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2026-10-25T08:06:33Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>vaccine</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:label>Brucella melitensis and Brucella abortus L7/L12 and truncated Omp31 subunit vaccine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009355 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009355">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001221"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0000208"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0000624"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001011"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_11077"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0001243"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9913"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0003355"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_235"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0003390"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_10090"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Brucella abortus subunit vaccine using recombinant proteins omp19 and P39 were used individually and combined as a cocktail for intraperitoneal immunization. Romp19+rp39 cocktail induced significantly higher protection against b. Abortus 544 and b. Melitensis 16M infection compared to individual proteins, with log units of protection in spleen and liver significantly greater in the cocktail group. Cocktail induced higher antibody titers with th1 predominant isotypes (igg2a/2b), significant splenocyte proliferation, and increased pro-inflammatory cytokines (ifn-γ, il-2, il-12). Anti-romp19+rp39 polysera enhanced macrophage viability against bacterial challenge more effectively than individual protein antisera.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117> Jie Zheng</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>VaxAgent </obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26826463</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2026-10-25T08:06:33Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>vaccine</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:label>Brucella abortus Omp19 and P39 subunit vaccine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009356 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/VO_0009356">
