        <obo:IAO_0000115>Brucella abortus DNA vaccine using two molecular vaccines were constructed: a recombinant adenovirus vaccine and a plasmid DNA vaccine co-expressing P39 and lumazine synthase proteins. Dna priming followed by adenovirus boosting strategy significantly reduced the numbers of Brucella abortus in the mouse model. Dna prime and adenovirus boost immunization induced robust humoral and cellular.</obo:IAO_0000115>
