            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Brucella melitensis recombinant vector vaccine using the multi-epitope construct was linked with gpgpg, aay, and KK linkers, cloned into the pet-32a shuttle vector using bamhi and hindiii restriction sites, and expressed as a soluble ∼82 kda protein in escherichia coli shuffle host. Construct showed stable interaction with bovine TLR4 and TLR9 receptors, suggesting potential to induce. Vaccine is predicted to stimulate t- and b-cell responses by presenting multiple epitopes and activating innate immunity via TLR4 and TLR9 agonism, potentially inducing ifn-γ production.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117> Jie Zheng</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>VaxAgent </obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36927475</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2026-10-25T08:06:33Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>vaccine</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:label>Brucella melitensis and Brucella abortus virB10 Omp31 Omp16 recombinant vector vaccine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


